1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,520
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:18,223
Cinderella and the Glass Slipper!

7
00:00:22,796 --> 00:00:27,487
Once upon a time, in a little
town surrounded by green hills,

8
00:00:27,546 --> 00:00:31,362
there lived a very kind
and hardworking girl.

9
00:00:32,007 --> 00:00:36,559
Her father, a gentle merchant
who traveled very far away,

10
00:00:36,618 --> 00:00:40,309
had married again, to a very proud lady.

11
00:00:40,981 --> 00:00:45,014
The stepmother had two daughters, and
both of them only thought about new

12
00:00:45,064 --> 00:00:48,909
dresses, perfumes, and fancy hairstyles.

13
00:00:49,547 --> 00:00:54,052
Meanwhile, the girl swept the
whole house, washed the dishes,

14
00:00:54,102 --> 00:00:58,155
and looked after the fire in the
fireplace from early in the morning.

15
00:00:58,802 --> 00:01:03,369
At the end of the day, she sat
close to the warm ashes to rest,

16
00:01:03,427 --> 00:01:06,910
and her face was always
smudged with cinders.

17
00:01:07,548 --> 00:01:10,970
That is why the stepsisters
began to call her Cinderella,

18
00:01:11,020 --> 00:01:13,809
which means the little cinder girl.

19
00:01:14,427 --> 00:01:19,919
Even so, Cinderella stayed sweet and
cheerful, and she never answered back

20
00:01:19,969 --> 00:01:21,966
with an unkind word.

21
00:01:22,631 --> 00:01:26,378
Her only friend was a little
brown owl with a red bow,

22
00:01:26,519 --> 00:01:28,614
who lived by the attic window.

23
00:01:29,188 --> 00:01:30,565
Hoo, hoo!

24
00:01:30,664 --> 00:01:35,352
Good evening, Cinderella, I came
here just to keep you company,

25
00:01:35,402 --> 00:01:38,885
Popcorn said, blinking her little eyes.

26
00:01:39,965 --> 00:01:44,643
One morning, somebody knocked very
loudly on the front door of the house.

27
00:01:46,382 --> 00:01:51,110
It was a messenger from the palace,
carrying a golden envelope with the royal

28
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:52,360
seal.

29
00:01:52,675 --> 00:01:56,734
Our prince invites every young lady
in town to a grand ball at the palace,

30
00:01:56,784 --> 00:01:57,946
tomorrow night,

31
00:01:57,996 --> 00:02:01,563
the palace messenger
announced in a loud voice.

32
00:02:02,202 --> 00:02:07,110
The two stepsisters hopped with joy and
spent the whole day choosing ribbons,

33
00:02:07,160 --> 00:02:09,241
gloves, and necklaces.

34
00:02:09,879 --> 00:02:13,434
I would love to go to the ball too, even
if it were only to see the music and

35
00:02:13,484 --> 00:02:14,425
the lights,

36
00:02:14,475 --> 00:02:16,542
Cinderella said softly.

37
00:02:17,191 --> 00:02:22,044
The stepmother tossed a whole bowl of
lentils into the ashes and gave the girl

38
00:02:22,094 --> 00:02:24,161
a very hard task.

39
00:02:24,782 --> 00:02:29,399
If you can pick every single lentil
out of those ashes before nightfall,

40
00:02:29,449 --> 00:02:31,440
then we can talk about this ball,

41
00:02:31,490 --> 00:02:35,001
the stepmother replied,
with her nose in the air.

42
00:02:35,657 --> 00:02:39,968
So Popcorn called the little birds from
the garden, and they came flying in

43
00:02:40,018 --> 00:02:41,585
through the kitchen window.

44
00:02:42,227 --> 00:02:46,913
Together they picked out the lentils
one by one, and the bowl was full again

45
00:02:46,963 --> 00:02:48,822
before the sun went down.

46
00:02:49,464 --> 00:02:54,873
But even so, the stepmother and the
stepsisters climbed into the carriage and

47
00:02:54,923 --> 00:02:57,642
left for the ball without Cinderella.

48
00:03:00,527 --> 00:03:04,852
Cinderella went out to the garden,
looked up at the first stars,

49
00:03:04,902 --> 00:03:07,052
and let a tiny tear fall.

50
00:03:14,146 --> 00:03:19,657
Suddenly, a golden light began to shine
among the rose bushes in the garden.

51
00:03:23,252 --> 00:03:26,805
In the middle of the light
appeared a lady with silver hair,

52
00:03:26,877 --> 00:03:30,763
a lavender cloak, and a
little wand in her hand.

53
00:03:31,371 --> 00:03:36,875
Don't cry, my dear, I am your fairy
godmother, and I have come to help you go

54
00:03:36,925 --> 00:03:37,908
to the ball,

55
00:03:37,958 --> 00:03:41,802
the fairy godmother said
in a very gentle voice.

56
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:43,765
Hoo, hoo!

57
00:03:43,878 --> 00:03:47,865
I just knew that something wonderful
was going to happen tonight,

58
00:03:47,915 --> 00:03:50,856
Popcorn whispered, very excited.

59
00:03:51,487 --> 00:03:56,562
The fairy godmother asked for the biggest
pumpkin in the vegetable garden and

60
00:03:56,612 --> 00:03:58,929
touched it with the tip of her wand.

61
00:04:02,506 --> 00:04:07,831
At once, the pumpkin grew and grew,
and it turned into a beautiful golden

62
00:04:07,881 --> 00:04:10,420
carriage with shining wheels.

63
00:04:11,052 --> 00:04:15,835
Then six little grey mice from the
pantry turned into six white horses with

64
00:04:15,885 --> 00:04:18,397
soft, silky manes.

65
00:04:19,033 --> 00:04:23,266
Two little lizards from the garden
turned into two elegant footmen,

66
00:04:23,505 --> 00:04:25,794
ready to open the carriage door.

67
00:04:26,432 --> 00:04:32,298
At last, the fairy touched Cinderella's
apron, and it became a gold and silver

68
00:04:32,348 --> 00:04:35,304
gown embroidered with tiny stars.

69
00:04:38,877 --> 00:04:42,291
On the girl's feet appeared
a pair of glass slippers,

70
00:04:42,363 --> 00:04:45,472
the most delicate in the whole wide world.

71
00:04:46,063 --> 00:04:50,559
Go and have a wonderful time, but remember
that the magic ends when the clock

72
00:04:50,609 --> 00:04:52,003
strikes midnight,

73
00:04:52,158 --> 00:04:54,946
the fairy godmother warned her kindly.

74
00:04:56,052 --> 00:05:00,350
The golden carriage rolled across the
town and stopped right in front of the

75
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,036
glowing palace.

76
00:05:04,961 --> 00:05:10,203
When Cinderella walked into the ballroom,
the music grew softer and everybody

77
00:05:10,253 --> 00:05:11,486
stopped to look.

78
00:05:12,117 --> 00:05:17,123
The prince crossed the ballroom, bowed
politely, and invited the mysterious

79
00:05:17,173 --> 00:05:19,017
young lady to dance.

80
00:05:19,643 --> 00:05:23,085
Would you like to dance this waltz with
me, under the lights of the ballroom?

81
00:05:23,135 --> 00:05:25,771
the prince asked with a shy smile.

82
00:05:26,377 --> 00:05:31,619
The two of them danced all evening
long, and Cinderella felt as light as a

83
00:05:31,669 --> 00:05:32,971
little feather.

84
00:05:33,632 --> 00:05:39,123
Not even the stepsisters recognized
Cinderella, in that sparkling gown and

85
00:05:39,173 --> 00:05:41,754
with her face so clean.

86
00:05:42,384 --> 00:05:47,181
Even so, she walked over to them and
offered them the sweet oranges that the

87
00:05:47,231 --> 00:05:48,881
prince had brought for her.

88
00:05:49,508 --> 00:05:54,208
The stepsisters were surprised by so
much kindness, and they thought that the

89
00:05:54,258 --> 00:05:57,519
young lady must be a princess
from another kingdom.

90
00:05:58,624 --> 00:06:03,088
The party was so lovely that Cinderella
did not even notice the evening

91
00:06:03,138 --> 00:06:04,441
passing by.

92
00:06:05,094 --> 00:06:09,702
Suddenly, the great clock in the
tower began to strike midnight.

93
00:06:16,531 --> 00:06:19,917
Cinderella remembered the
fairy godmother's warning,

94
00:06:19,990 --> 00:06:24,278
said a quick goodbye, and ran
down the palace staircase.

95
00:06:27,162 --> 00:06:31,668
In her hurry, one of the glass slippers
slipped off her foot and was left

96
00:06:31,718 --> 00:06:34,229
behind on a marble step.

97
00:06:34,876 --> 00:06:39,618
The prince ran after her, but all he
found was the little slipper shining on

98
00:06:39,668 --> 00:06:41,026
the staircase.

99
00:06:41,685 --> 00:06:45,460
On the road, the carriage
turned back into a pumpkin,

100
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:50,488
the horses turned back into mice, and
the gown turned back into an apron.

101
00:06:51,149 --> 00:06:54,716
Only the other glass slipper
stayed on Cinderella's foot,

102
00:06:54,816 --> 00:06:56,758
safe and shining.

103
00:06:57,355 --> 00:06:58,731
Hoo, hoo!

104
00:06:58,856 --> 00:07:03,473
Come with me, Cinderella, I
know the shortest way back home,

105
00:07:03,523 --> 00:07:06,534
Popcorn said, flying ahead of her.

106
00:07:13,606 --> 00:07:18,770
The next morning, the rooster crowed
very early on the palace roof.

107
00:07:21,338 --> 00:07:25,538
The prince could not think about anything
else except the kind young lady in

108
00:07:25,588 --> 00:07:26,974
the golden gown.

109
00:07:27,621 --> 00:07:31,768
I will find the owner of this glass
slipper, even if I have to visit every

110
00:07:31,818 --> 00:07:33,515
single house in the kingdom,

111
00:07:33,565 --> 00:07:35,256
the prince said firmly.

112
00:07:35,923 --> 00:07:40,873
So the palace messenger went out into
the town, carrying the slipper on a red

113
00:07:40,923 --> 00:07:42,351
velvet cushion.

114
00:07:43,007 --> 00:07:46,818
He visited one house after another,
and many young ladies tried on the

115
00:07:46,868 --> 00:07:49,851
slipper, but it did not fit any of them.

116
00:07:50,951 --> 00:07:55,865
At last, the messenger knocked on
the door of Cinderella's house.

117
00:07:57,607 --> 00:08:02,015
The older stepsister tried on the slipper
first, but her foot would not fit in

118
00:08:02,065 --> 00:08:03,265
it at all.

119
00:08:03,634 --> 00:08:07,626
The younger stepsister tried
too, as hard as she could,

120
00:08:07,676 --> 00:08:10,673
but the slipper was still
much too small for her.

121
00:08:11,313 --> 00:08:15,735
Then Cinderella came out of the
kitchen, wiped her hands on her apron,

122
00:08:15,785 --> 00:08:18,144
and spoke very politely.

123
00:08:18,802 --> 00:08:21,676
May I please try on that
little slipper too, kind sir?

124
00:08:21,726 --> 00:08:23,793
Cinderella asked gently.

125
00:08:24,454 --> 00:08:29,306
The stepsisters began to laugh, but the
messenger said that every young lady

126
00:08:29,356 --> 00:08:31,562
in town had the right to try.

127
00:08:32,218 --> 00:08:36,960
Cinderella sat down on a chair, and
the glass slipper slid onto her foot

128
00:08:37,010 --> 00:08:38,210
perfectly.

129
00:08:38,803 --> 00:08:42,064
Then she took the other slipper
out of her apron pocket,

130
00:08:42,178 --> 00:08:46,759
exactly like the first one,
and everyone's mouth fell open.

131
00:08:47,400 --> 00:08:52,448
At that very moment, the fairy godmother
appeared and turned the apron back

132
00:08:52,498 --> 00:08:55,036
into the gold and silver gown.

133
00:08:59,082 --> 00:09:04,448
The two stepsisters felt very ashamed,
knelt down, and said sorry for

134
00:09:04,498 --> 00:09:06,051
everything they had done.

135
00:09:06,700 --> 00:09:11,242
I forgive you with all my heart, and
I hope that from now on we can be true

136
00:09:11,292 --> 00:09:12,115
friends,

137
00:09:12,165 --> 00:09:15,510
Cinderella said, hugging her stepsisters.

138
00:09:16,198 --> 00:09:20,237
From that day on, the
stepsisters learned to be kind,

139
00:09:20,295 --> 00:09:23,445
and they began to help with
the chores around the house.

140
00:09:24,086 --> 00:09:28,105
The prince and Cinderella had a
wedding party in the palace garden,

141
00:09:28,155 --> 00:09:31,097
full of flowers, music, and cake.

142
00:09:31,750 --> 00:09:36,145
Popcorn landed on the palace
window, straightened her red bow,

143
00:09:36,195 --> 00:09:38,984
and watched the party, full of joy.

144
00:09:39,592 --> 00:09:40,968
Hoo, hoo!

145
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:46,128
Kindness and forgiveness make our hearts
light, and gentleness always finds

146
00:09:46,178 --> 00:09:47,020
its way,

147
00:09:47,070 --> 00:09:50,470
Popcorn said in her soft and sweet voice.

148
00:09:51,116 --> 00:09:57,155
And Cinderella lived happily ever
after, always kind to everyone she met.

149
00:10:04,432 --> 00:10:05,632
The End.

150
00:10:07,339 --> 00:10:08,051
Hoo...

151
00:10:08,101 --> 00:10:09,125
Psst!

152
00:10:09,175 --> 00:10:10,747
Are you still awake?

153
00:10:10,901 --> 00:10:12,955
Did you like tonight's story?

154
00:10:13,089 --> 00:10:18,130
Cinderella and Popcorn showed us that
kindness and forgiveness make our hearts

155
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:21,900
light, and that gentleness
always finds its way.

156
00:10:22,183 --> 00:10:26,489
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

157
00:10:26,785 --> 00:10:31,683
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

158
00:10:31,733 --> 00:10:34,138
for more stories at bedtime.

159
00:10:34,442 --> 00:10:35,642
Hoo...

